WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.669
PayPatch helps an accounts-payable agent carry an exporter lesson
into the next invoice.

2
00:00:06.689 --> 00:00:10.422
This blue workbench uses fictional business data.

3
00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:15.114
Start with invoice INV-202 and empty history.

4
00:00:15.134 --> 00:00:21.992
Click Stage draft: the runtime records a hold, because the
counterparty field needs clarification.

5
00:00:23.092 --> 00:00:27.876
On the left, INV-101 shows the earlier cold session.

6
00:00:27.896 --> 00:00:35.417
Two fresh gpt-6.1-sol agents ran identical instructions in the
recorded experiment.

7
00:00:35.437 --> 00:00:41.025
The cold agent chose HOLD, and its sandbox ledger executed that
action.

8
00:00:41.045 --> 00:00:48.824
Today's editable workbench runs a deterministic policy; those model
generations remain recorded evidence.

9
00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:53.684
Now recall the experience in Recorded proof mode.

10
00:00:53.704 --> 00:00:58.288
The returned lesson names ref_b as the contract counterparty field.

11
00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:03.248
It combines the executed hold receipt with trusted exporter
feedback.

12
00:01:03.268 --> 00:01:10.376
Encrypted Walrus Memory carries this general rule forward; today's
directory supplies the recipient.

13
00:01:11.476 --> 00:01:14.563
Switch to Live mainnet and recall again.

14
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:26.443
This click makes a new, read-only account check through Tatum's Sui
Gateway GraphQL, followed by actual native SDK retrieval from the
original learning namespace.

15
00:01:26.463 --> 00:01:33.320
The authorized delegate reads the same completed Walrus experience,
with today's read timestamp.

16
00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:38.107
Return to the current invoice and stage the draft.

17
00:01:38.127 --> 00:01:42.470
The learned field, ref_b, points to R91.

18
00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:51.382
Today's directory resolves that reference to demo:fir, so INV-202
stages 9,800 minor units.

19
00:01:51.402 --> 00:01:55.496
The amount and identity come directly from the current input.

20
00:01:56.596 --> 00:02:03.512
Change R91's recipient to demo:maple, and the amount to 4,721.

21
00:02:03.532 --> 00:02:08.231
Stage again: the receipt shows a new current-directory draft.

22
00:02:08.251 --> 00:02:19.166
Open Memory provenance to inspect the original blob identifier,
observed receipt, GraphQL account transport, and active, authorized
delegate.

23
00:02:19.186 --> 00:02:21.992
The exporter lesson stays ref_b.

24
00:02:23.092 --> 00:02:32.948
Below, inspect the two-session evidence: identical instructions,
empty versus recalled history, and executed hold-to-draft results.

25
00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:40.711
Ten earlier pilot memories plus one observed learning experience
completed on mainnet, in separate namespaces.

26
00:02:40.731 --> 00:02:47.312
Follow the technical article and public source to reproduce the
receipts and explore the learning loop.
